MiniCPM-OCR-Decision-2B for LiteRT

The LiteRT graphs (*.tflite) and the tables (tables/tables.safetensors) in this repository are converted from openbmb/MiniCPM-OCR-Jev, revision a0ed278eb6aa1f333a711665ab610055a4a816ab (https://huggingface.co/openbmb/MiniCPM-OCR-Jev), by OpenBMB, licensed under the Apache License 2.0. LICENSE is a copy of the LICENSE file of github.com/OpenBMB/MiniCPM-OCR at commit 8177040f0d6c824ccf87bc18b938b6a0f91b6d0e, which that model's card names. Every graph and the tables are derived from that repository's model.safetensors: the changes are listed in REPRODUCE.md. That model was trained from Qwen/Qwen3.5-2B (https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.5-2B), licensed under the Apache License 2.0. tokenizer.json is the source repository's file, unchanged.

The Python host (host/) is a numpy port of what the source's score path does: the prompt and the token checks of scripts/minicpm-ocr-jev/eval/score.py (github.com/OpenBMB/MiniCPM-OCR, Apache License 2.0); the picture preprocessing, position tables and rotary tables of transformers (Apache License 2.0), including PyTorch's uint8 antialiased bicubic resize (BSD 3-Clause License). Its tokenizer runs on the tokenizers library (Apache License 2.0), and the graphs run on LiteRT (ai-edge-litert, Apache License 2.0).

The conversion scripts (conversion/) run the model code of transformers with litert-torch, ai-edge-quantizer and LiteRT, each licensed under the Apache License 2.0. conversion/patch_q35.py derives from LiteRT Torch and keeps its copyright header.

No picture or text of a benchmark is in this repository. examples/run_example.py downloads the source's three official examples at run time from the commit above; their pictures are crops of OmniDocBench pages, which that project offers for research use only. examples/score_olmocr_set.py and conversion/fetch_inputs.py download records of openbmb/JevOCRBench at run time, on your disk: only its olmOCR family, which derives from olmOCR-bench (https://huggingface.co/datasets/allenai/olmOCR-bench), Open Data Commons Attribution License v1.0 (https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/by/1-0/). Poznanski et al., "olmOCR: Unlocking Trillions of Tokens in PDFs with Vision Language Models," arXiv:2502.18443 (2025), https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.18443. That benchmark's DATA_LICENSE.md and NOTICE give the terms of its records, and copyright in the underlying documents stays with their holders. conversion/sets/ holds only record ids and sizes.

